 "id": "carried-over-orders",
 "kind": "topic",
 "not_established": [
  "Why any order was still open on 30 June, or why one was closed without being paid. Neither is in a ledger.",
  "Whether carrying orders is why a year’s spending looks off against its vote. What is measured is how far moving them back shifts it.",
  "Which year’s money an invoice truly belonged to beyond the order it drew down: an invoice can differ from the amount it liquidated.",
  "Whether an order closed with nothing paid was bought again on a new order. The journal ties a payment to its order, never one order to the one before it; in a revolving fund, Nature’s Classroom’s carried order was closed and the same amount paid on a new one.",
  "What FY2026 will carry out: its close is not in this run."
 ],
